{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Which references admit the pair κ-family K_κ? (2026-10-13)\n\nQuestion (NEXT.md 2k, plan §3): for which product references $\\langle(v\\otimes u)^L|$ ($v\\cdot u=0$, the Borel orbit $\\langle\\mathrm{vac}|\\rho(g)$ of $\\mathrm{vac}=e_1\\otimes e_4$) do the pair-1 words $\\{1,X_1,X_2,X_3,X_3X_1\\}$ ($X_1=t_1(\\theta_F)$, $X_2=t_2(\\theta_F+h)$, $X_3=\\hat t_3(\\theta_F+h)$) contain a **common group rotation** of pair 1, $[v(1-\\kappa\\Lambda)]\\otimes[u(1-\\kappa\\Lambda)^{-1}]$, at the ABJM point with $z_2=z_3$? In particular: the twisted vacuum $\\langle 0_w|$ (companion-frame eigenbra of $t^{G_c(w)}$), whose diagonal-frame image is $v_j=\\lambda_j\\prod_{m\\ne j}(w_1-z_m)$, $u_j=\\prod_{m\\le3}(z_j-w_m)$.\n\nConventions: chain A F A F (site 1 leftmost), bras row vectors, $\\psi\\to\\psi.M$; $\\rho_A(E_{ij})=e_{ij}$, $\\rho_F(E_{ij})=-e_{ji}$; $T=L_1\\cdots L_{2L}G$; fused single-pass $t_k$ as in `pair-group-rotation.wb` (same code, symbols prefixed `ra`). ABJM point $\\theta=(\\theta_{F,n}+2h,\\theta_{F,n})$, $h=1/2$, $\\theta_F=(-3/5,-11/8,-7/9)$, $z=(3/2,5/4,5/4,4/7)$, $a=1/3$. All arithmetic exact (rational / symbolic) unless marked.\n\nKernel discipline: shared kernel, all globals prefixed `ra`, L ≤ 3 pairs.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary of results (2026-10-13; full report `notes/agent-2026-10-13-reference-map.md`)\n\n1. **Twisted vacuum $\\langle0_w|$.** At $z_2=z_3$ its diagonal-frame image degenerates, $v\\to(0,1,-1,0)$ (A site frozen, independent of $w$), $u=u_w$ generic. A common pair rotation exists on this limit reference (rank-3 span, all $\\kappa$-components in the span; L = 2, 3 exact mod p, §7) but it is an **F-site rotation only**, realised by $K^F_\\kappa=[1-\\kappa e_1'+\\kappa^2e_2']+2\\kappa X_1+8\\kappa^2X_2$ (symbolic check §9c), **not** by the 5-word $K_\\kappa$ of $W_a$. At $z_2\\ne z_3$ no $\\kappa$-family exists unless $w_1\\in\\{z_j\\}$ ($v=e_a$ frozen; §9b): dim(span $\\cap$ span of the 13 $\\kappa$-components) = 2 (§5e).\n2. **Admissible set at $z_2=z_3$** ($p=(v_2,v_3)$, $q=(u_2,u_3)$; §5, §5c): $\\{v_1u_1=0,\\ v_4u_4=0,\\ p\\cdot q=0\\}$ (block-BPS: $v|_C\\cdot u|_C=0$ in every spectral block of $\\Lambda$) $\\ \\cup\\ \\{p=q=0\\}$ (both sites on indices $\\{1,4\\}$: torus images of $W_a$). At generic $z$ only the block condition ($v_ju_j=0\\ \\forall j$; §9b). Inside the Borel orbit: $\\{v_4=0,u_1=0,p\\cdot q=0\\}\\cup\\{p=q=0\\}$.\n3. **GL(4) covariance (§6):** $G'=g^{-T}\\Lambda g^T$; admissible $\\Leftrightarrow$ $[G'^n]_{41}=0$ ($n=1,2,3$) or $G'=\\Lambda+cE_{41}$.\n4. **No-go:** all admissible references except the W-type have vanishing cross-block pairings $p_{23}=p_{32}=0$; $W_a$ is special because $v_1u_1=-v_4u_4\\ne0$.\n5. **Untwisting (§8):** $D=\\mathrm{diag}(c-\\varphi_j)$ for $\\kappa=1-c\\varepsilon$ (not $c+\\varphi_j$); at $\\varphi_2=\\varphi_3$ the pair collapses to $(0,1,-1,0)\\otimes(\\hat u_j/(c-\\varphi_j))$. Near the degeneration ($z_2-z_3=\\varepsilon\\Delta\\varphi$) the best-fit residual is linear in $\\Delta\\varphi$, independent of $\\varepsilon$, and has a charged part for the twisted vacuum (§5f).\n\nStatus: all cells were (re)run in the shared Wolfram kernel after its restart at 08:03; the exact python versions in `checks/session-2026-10-13/refmap/` (written while the kernel was down) agree with every Wolfram output (section 10).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Setup: fused single-pass transfer matrices (port of `pair-group-rotation.wb`, prefix `ra`)\n\n$t_k(u)=\\prod_s g_s(u)\\,\\mathrm{tr}[L^{(k)}_1\\cdots L^{(k)}_N\\wedge^kG]$, $L^{(k)}_s=(u-\\tilde\\theta_s)+h\\sum_{ab}D_k(e_{ab})\\otimes\\rho_s(E_{ab})$, $\\tilde\\theta_A=\\theta$, $\\tilde\\theta_F=\\theta+(k-1)h$, $g_A=\\prod_{j=1}^{k-1}(u-\\theta-jh)$, $g_F=\\prod_{j=0}^{k-2}(u-\\theta-jh)$; `reg -> True` drops exactly vanishing scalar factors ($\\hat t_k$). `raTdef` = quantum-minor definition (calibration). `raLam[k,u,thRest]` = localisation constant $\\lambda_k$ over pairs 2..L.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "rah = 1/2;\nraId4 = IdentityMatrix[4, SparseArray];\nraE[i_, j_] := SparseArray[{{i, j} -> 1}, {4, 4}];\nraRho[\"A\"][a_, b_] := raE[a, b];\nraRho[\"F\"][a_, b_] := -raE[b, a];\nraD[k_] := raD[k] = Module[{eps}, Table[D[Minors[IdentityMatrix[4] + eps Normal[raE[a, b]], k], eps] /. eps -> 0, {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];\nraThT[ty_, k_, t_] := If[ty == \"A\", t, t + (k - 1) rah];\nraDropZeros[fs_List] := DeleteCases[fs, x_ /; TrueQ[x == 0]];\nraGfac[ty_, k_, u_, t_, reg_] := Module[{fs},\n   fs = If[ty == \"A\", Table[u - t - j rah, {j, 1, k - 1}], Table[u - t - j rah, {j, 0, k - 2}]];\n   Times @@ If[TrueQ[reg], raDropZeros[fs], fs]];\nraLax[k_, ty_, u_, t_] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k]},\n   Table[(u - raThT[ty, k, t]) KroneckerDelta[i, j] raId4 + rah Sum[raD[k][[a, b, i, j]] raRho[ty][a, b], {a, 4}, {b, 4}], {i, n}, {j, n}]];\nraT[k_, u_, types_, th_, G_, reg_: False] := Module[{n = Binomial[4, k], mon, lx, wG, pref},\n   If[k == 0, Return[IdentityMatrix[4^Length[types], SparseArray]]];\n   mon = raLax[k, types[[1]], u, th[[1]]];\n   Do[lx = raLax[k, types[[s]], u, th[[s]]];\n    mon = Table[Sum[KroneckerProduct[mon[[i, m]], lx[[m, j]]], {m, n}], {i, n}, {j, n}], {s, 2, Length[types]}];\n   wG = Minors[G, k];\n   pref = Times @@ Table[raGfac[types[[s]], k, u, th[[s]], reg], {s, Length[types]}];\n   pref Sum[mon[[i, j]] wG[[j, i]], {i, n}, {j, n}]];\nraUV[i_] := UnitVector[4, i];\nraProd[vs_List] := Flatten[Fold[KroneckerProduct, First[vs], Rest[vs]]];\nraW[a_] := {raUV[1] + a raUV[4], raUV[4] - a raUV[1]};\nraSplit[psi_, rest_] := Module[{m = ArrayReshape[Normal[psi], {16, Length[rest]}], p}, p = (m . rest)/(rest . rest); {p, m - Outer[Times, p, rest]}];\nraLam[k_, u_, thRest_List] := Times @@ raDropZeros[Flatten[Table[If[OddQ[s], Table[u - thRest[[s]] - j rah, {j, 0, k - 1}],\n       Join[{u - thRest[[s]] - k rah}, Table[u - thRest[[s]] - j rah, {j, 0, k - 2}]]], {s, Length[thRest]}]]];\nraMon1[u_, types_, th_, G_] := Module[{mon = raLax[1, types[[1]], u, th[[1]]], lx},\n   Do[lx = raLax[1, types[[s]], u, th[[s]]]; mon = Table[Sum[KroneckerProduct[mon[[i, m]], lx[[m, j]]], {m, 4}], {i, 4}, {j, 4}], {s, 2, Length[types]}];\n   Table[Sum[mon[[i, m]] G[[m, j]], {m, 4}], {i, 4}, {j, 4}]];\nraTdef[k_, u_, types_, th_, G_] := Module[{ts = Table[raMon1[u - m rah, types, th, G], {m, 0, k - 1}]},\n   Sum[Sum[Signature[p] (Dot @@ Table[ts[[m, ss[[p[[m]]]], ss[[m]]]], {m, k}]), {p, Permutations[Range[k]]}], {ss, Subsets[Range[4], {k}]}]];\nraG0 = {{3/2, -1/3, 2, 1/5}, {1, 2/7, -1, 3}, {-2/3, 1, 1/2, 1}, {1/4, -1, 5/3, -2}};\nraCal = Table[{k, Max[Abs[Flatten[Normal[raT[k, 37/100, {\"A\", \"F\"}, {2/7, -3/5}, raG0] - raTdef[k, 37/100, {\"A\", \"F\"}, {2/7, -3/5}, raG0]]]]]}, {k, 1, 4}];\nGrid[Prepend[raCal, {\"k\", \"max |fused t_k - quantum-minor t_k| (exact, 1 pair, random twist raG0)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
