  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5c. The admissible set in closed form and its test (sub-families of the Borel orbit and its closure)\n\nFrom the symbolic `Reduce` table of §5 (all seven Levi representatives of $v$) the admissible set at $z_2=z_3$ is, with $p=(v_2,v_3)$, $q=(u_2,u_3)$ and $v\\cdot u=0$,\n\n$$\\mathcal A=\\mathcal A_{\\rm block}\\cup\\mathcal A_W,\\qquad \\mathcal A_{\\rm block}=\\{v_1u_1=0,\\;v_4u_4=0,\\;p\\cdot q=0\\},\\qquad \\mathcal A_W=\\{p=q=0\\}.$$\n\n$\\mathcal A_{\\rm block}$: $v$ and $u$ are BPS **inside every spectral block of $\\Lambda$** ($v|_C\\cdot u|_C=0$ for $C=\\{1\\},\\{2,3\\},\\{4\\}$, equivalently $u f(\\Lambda)v^T=0$ for every function $f$); $\\mathcal A_W$: both sites supported on the indices $\\{1,4\\}$ (the torus images of $W_a$, where $v_1u_1=-v_4u_4\\ne0$ is allowed). Below: the closed form is tested against the exact rank test on named sub-families and on random samples.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "raPred[v_, u_] := Module[{p = v[[{2, 3}]], q = u[[{2, 3}]]}, (v[[1]] u[[1]] == 0 && v[[4]] u[[4]] == 0 && p . q == 0) || (p == {0, 0} && q == {0, 0})];\nraRow2[name_, v_, u_] := Module[{t = raTest[v, u], pr = raPred[v, u]}, {name, v, u, TrueQ[v . u == 0], pr, t[[5]], pr === t[[5]], t[[1]], t[[3]]}];\nraHead2 = {\"reference (z2=z3 chain)\", \"v\", \"u\", \"v.u=0\", \"closed form predicts\", \"K_kappa exists (exact rank test, 3 kappas)\", \"agree\", \"rank of 5-word span\", \"# nonzero kappa-components\"};\nraScan2 = {\n  raRow2[\"Borel: W-type, v=(1,0,0,2), u=(-6,0,0,3)\", {1, 0, 0, 2}, {-6, 0, 0, 3}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: v=(1,0,0,v4), u generic (q != 0)\", {1, 0, 0, 2}, {-6, 1, 2, 3}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: v generic, u=(-v4,0,0,1)\", {1, -2/3, 5/7, 3/2}, {-3/2, 0, 0, 1}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: gl(2)-symmetric v=(1,2,2,3), u=(-4,1/4,1/4,1)\", {1, 2, 2, 3}, {-4, 1/4, 1/4, 1}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: gl(2)-symmetric v=(1,2,2,0), u=(0,0,0,1)\", {1, 2, 2, 0}, {0, 0, 0, 1}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: v=(1,2,3,0), u=(0,3,-2,5)  [p.q=0]\", {1, 2, 3, 0}, {0, 3, -2, 5}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: v=e1, u=(0,2,3,5)\", {1, 0, 0, 0}, {0, 2, 3, 5}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: v=(1,2,3,0), u=(-5,1,1,3)  [p.q=5]\", {1, 2, 3, 0}, {-5, 1, 1, 3}],\n  raRow2[\"Borel: v=(1,2,3,2), u=(-2,3,-2,1)  [p.q=0, v4 u4 != 0]\", {1, 2, 3, 2}, {-2, 3, -2, 1}],\n  raRow2[\"closure (u4=0): v=(1,2,3,2), u=(0,3,-2,0)\", {1, 2, 3, 2}, {0, 3, -2, 0}],\n  raRow2[\"closure (u4=0): only u2,u3 nonzero, v=(1,0,0,2), u=(0,5,7,0)\", {1, 0, 0, 2}, {0, 5, 7, 0}],\n  raRow2[\"closure (v1=0): v=(0,2,3,5), u=(7,3,-2,0)\", {0, 2, 3, 5}, {7, 3, -2, 0}],\n  raRow2[\"closure (v1=0): only v2,v3 nonzero, v=(0,2,3,0), u=(1,3,-2,4)\", {0, 2, 3, 0}, {1, 3, -2, 4}],\n  raRow2[\"closure: v=e4, u=(1,2,3,0)\", {0, 0, 0, 1}, {1, 2, 3, 0}]};\nGrid[Prepend[raScan2, raHead2], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
