  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 10. Python cross-check (`checks/session-2026-10-13/refmap/`, written while the kernel was down) vs the Wolfram outputs above\n\nThe python scripts (exact `Fraction`/`sympy`/mod p on top of `pgbase.py`/`eng.py`) were run first; every Wolfram cell of §5c-§9c was then run and **agrees**: §5c named rows (14/14 agree with the closed form) and random test (Wolfram: 44+20+142 samples, 0 disagreements; python 39+20+137, 0), §5e eigenvalues (symbolic True), generic-z obstruction table (rank 5, 13 components of rank 13, dim 2, |S| = 12 with rank 5, rank 6), §5f residuals (identical to 6 digits: e.g. $\\Delta\\varphi=0.1$, $\\varepsilon=10^{-4}$: 0.343292 / 0.161295 / 0.113858 / 0), §6 covariance ($G'=g^{-T}\\Lambda g^T$ only; $W_a$: $[G'^n]_{41}=-13/42,-377/588,-8749/8232$), §7 L = 3 (all 8 passing references: localisation and the K-identity for the three $\\kappa$ True; negative control: localisation True, no pair-level solution at two $\\kappa$), §8 untwisting (deviations 3.0e-2, 3.0e-3, 2.9e-4, 2.9e-5 for $D=c-\\varphi$; about 1 for $c+\\varphi$; $\\varphi_2=\\varphi_3$: 3.0e-2 ... 3.0e-5), §9 Lie algebra dimensions (2, 3, 2, 3, 3), §9b generic-z (117 patterns, 50 admissible = exactly the disjoint-support ones; twisted vacuum admissible only for $w_1=z_a$), §9c symbolic ($W_a$ and $K^F_\\kappa$ True; cross-applications False).\n\nAdditional python-only results (not ported): exhaustive scan over $(v,u)\\in\\{-1,0,1,2\\}^8$ with $v\\cdot u=0$ (8946 pairs): at $z_2=z_3$ 2690 admissible, 0 mismatches with the closed form; at generic $z$ 1890 admissible = exactly the 1890 blockwise ones (`smallint.py`). Symbolic coefficient families (`symR6.py`, `symR2.py`): A-frozen class $c_3=8\\kappa^2$, $c_1=1-\\kappa e_1'+\\kappa^2e_2'-\\tfrac38c_4yz_1z_4$, $c_2=2\\kappa-\\tfrac38c_5yz_1z_4$, $c_{4,5}$ free, $u$-independent; class $(1,1,0,0)\\otimes(0,0,u_3,u_4)$: coefficients rational in $\\kappa$ with a pole at $\\kappa=1/y$. $K^F_\\kappa$ on the chain (L = 2, 3, mod p) for $\\kappa=3/10,-7/5,7/4,2/9$ (`r6_l3.py`).",
